      <h2>Boiler not working? What should you check before you call?</h2>
      <p class="brx-answer">These take a few minutes and sometimes get the heating back on without a visit.</p>
      <ol class="brx-checks">
        <li><strong>Pressure.</strong> The gauge should read 1 to 1.5 bar when the heating is cold. Below 1 bar, most boilers stop.</li>
        <li><strong>Gas supply.</strong> Does the hob light? On a prepayment meter, check there is credit.</li>
        <li><strong>Power.</strong> Check the fused switch next to the boiler is on and the display is lit. Check your fuse box for a tripped switch.</li>
        <li><strong>Thermostat and timer.</strong> Turn the thermostat up and check the clock has not reset after a power cut. Check smart thermostat batteries.</li>
        <li><strong>Condensate pipe.</strong> In freezing weather, check the plastic pipe outside for ice.</li>
        <li><strong>Reset once.</strong> Press reset one time. If it locks out again, leave it and ring us with the error code.</li>
      </ol>
      <div class="brx-danger">
        <p><strong>Smell gas?</strong> Do not touch light switches. Open windows, turn the gas off at the meter if it is safe to, get everyone out and ring the National Gas Emergency number on <a href="tel:08001119999">0800 111 999</a>. Once it is made safe, we can repair the boiler.</p>
