      <p class="brx-answer">Most winter breakdowns can be avoided with a few simple habits.</p>
      <ol class="brx-checks">
        <li><strong>Get it serviced every year.</strong> A <a class="brx-link" href="/boiler-service-liverpool">boiler service</a> catches worn parts early and keeps most manufacturer warranties valid.</li>
        <li><strong>Check the pressure once a month.</strong> 1 to 1.5 bar when cold.</li>
        <li><strong>Run the heating for 15 minutes a month in summer.</strong> It stops the pump and valves seizing.</li>
        <li><strong>Lag the condensate pipe.</strong> Insulating the outside pipe stops it freezing.</li>
        <li><strong>Bleed radiators every autumn.</strong> Air in the system makes the boiler work harder.</li>
        <li><strong>Fit a magnetic filter.</strong> It catches sludge before it reaches the boiler. Radiators already cold at the bottom may need a <a class="brx-link" href="/power-flushing-liverpool">power flush</a>.</li>
